This is the first clean evidence in the recent chain that making publication the worker's smallest first action can preserve reviewable work through a blocked terminal verdict. It prevented the #164 loss pattern.

The architecture verdict does not change yet: this ordering was obeyed from prose, not enforced by a repository/runtime state gate. PR #166 itself remains PARTIAL_MODEL because marker provenance and negative coverage are incomplete. Preserve it as evidence toward, not proof of, publish-evidence-before-settle.

