New evidence after LOCAL_CHECKPOINT_HEAD_SPLIT recovery:
- task-bound continuity was remotely published before semantic code;
- implementation and report followed as separate commits;
- the previously proven self-hash/caller-promotion exploit is now rejected with byte-identical OUTCOME_CANDIDATE state;
- no completion authority is inferred from PR/report existence.

The durable publication path therefore survived after exact-head reconciliation. The remaining recovery-layer defect is narrower: the external reporter still posts EXECUTION_FINISHED without terminal TASK_* even when a complete three-stage evidence chain exists. Do not rerun the valid API-gate work to compensate. The next semantic obligation is issuer-authenticated positive certificate acceptance, not reporter settlement repair unless SYSTEM/META separately wins ranking.
